agent: There is already one current implementation for this architecture: **Northwind Restock Alerts**.
  **Title:** Scheduled Restock Alert Service
  **Summary:** A GitHub Actions scheduled workflow runs every Monday, queries the order service for stock levels and reorder points using a read-only token, and emails one restock alert to the warehouse lead.
  **Realizations:**
  - **Scheduler:** GitHub Actions scheduled workflow starts the check every Monday.
  - **Stock reader:** Order service read-only stock query identifies items at or below reorder points.
  - **Alert sender:** Email notification sends one alert to the warehouse lead.
  **Deployment:** Hosted GitHub Actions runner using a scheduled workflow. It is not running yet.
  **Data:** Stock levels and reorder points move from the order service to the workflow; no customer or payment data is handled.
  **Security:** The workflow uses a read-only stock-query token stored as a secret.
  **Operations:** Depends on order service availability; failed-run detection and alerting are not defined.
  **Deployed by:** GitHub Actions
  **Why it matters:** highway-codify will use GitHub Actions to get Scheduled Restock Alert Service up and running.
  **Managed by:** GitHub Actions
  **Why it matters:** highway-codify will use GitHub Actions for managing Scheduled Restock Alert Service once it’s running.
  **Language:** None
  **Why it matters:** highway-codify will treat this as a Platform to manage as opposed to a coding project to write.
  **Capabilities:**
  - **Weekly restock alert:** Realized by GitHub Actions and email.
  - **Reorder point check:** Realized by the order service stock query.
  **Variation choices:** GitHub Actions is the scheduler; email is the alert channel; the schedule is every Monday, with the run time unspecified.
  **Realized interfaces:**
  - Read-only stock query: Compatible with the architecture.
  - Notification message: Compatible via email to the warehouse lead.
  **Conformance evidence:** The proposed workflow covers all stated responsibilities and preserves weekly scheduling, read-only stock access, and one alert per run.
  **Limitations:** The workflow is not yet running, and failed-run ownership/monitoring is not defined.
  **Technology choice:** GitHub Actions scheduled workflow — to run the weekly hosted job; chosen because it is an existing pipeline platform and matches the hosted-runner deployment pattern; evidence is the accepted architecture and the requested design.
  What would you add, correct, or remove?
  If this is accurate, just say so.
